/**
@page headers_insert_remove Inserting and removing headers

BONet can push or pop a VLAN tag or MPLS label, wrap the packet in an outer IPv4
or IPv6 header, insert an SRH after an IPv6 header, and remove a base IPv4 or
IPv6 header. Inserts are anchored on the Ethernet view, except the SRH, which is
anchored on an IPv6 view.

@code{.c}
bnt_eth__insert_vlan(&eth, 0x8100, 100);
bnt_eth__insert_ipv4(&eth, IPPROTO_IPIP, saddr, daddr);   /* outer encapsulation */
@endcode

@section headers_invalidation Re-parse after a change

After an insert or remove, views for headers past the change are no longer valid;
re-parse them before use. Views for headers before the change stay valid.

@code{.c}
SEC("xdp")
int push_vlan(struct xdp_md *ctx)
{
    bnt_eth  eth;
    bnt_ipv4 ip;

    if (bnt_eth__parse(ctx, 0, &eth))            return XDP_DROP;
    if (bnt_eth__insert_vlan(&eth, 0x8100, 100)) return XDP_DROP;

    /* eth is before the change and stays valid; navigate again from it. */
    if (bnt_eth__next_ipv4(&eth, &ip))           return XDP_DROP;

    return XDP_PASS;
}
@endcode
*/
